                                        "entry_id": "06b16d09-e115-31d2-a6d5-c7ac12da47d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One quadrillion (10¹⁵, or 1,000,000,000,000,000) bytes or 1,000 terabytes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d56aa7d-cdb2-31fb-9383-a3b6b407fea5",
                                        "entry_id": "06b16d09-e115-31d2-a6d5-c7ac12da47d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pebibyte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2b8962d-face-49bf-86fb-fa1e2891be08",
                                                "sense_id": "5d56aa7d-cdb2-31fb-9383-a3b6b407fea5",
                                                "text": "As we moved along that progression, we went from the folder analogy to the file cabinet analogy to the library analogy to — well, at petabytes we ran out of organizational analogies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f196dc43-37d7-41d6-a613-828448b559d0",
                                                "sense_id": "5d56aa7d-cdb2-31fb-9383-a3b6b407fea5",
                                                "text": "The Hadron Collider has gone from producing 320 terabytes of data a week to a petabyte a second. In short, it has been said that the total amount of data created worldwide in 2011 was about one zetabyte^([sic]) (or 1,000,000 petabytes) and that this figure will increase by 50%–60% in each subsequent year."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
